WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:06.970
Another milestone in the earthquake recovery
process was celebrated this morning in Kaiapoi,

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.420
with the ceremonial handover of regeneration
land ownership from the Crown to Waimakariri

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.740
District Council and Te Kōhaka o Tūhaitara
Trust.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.350
The Minister for Greater Christchurch Regeneration,
the Honourable Megan Woods, acknowledged the

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.760
importance of the occasion to our local communities.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:31.560
This is about land going back to local ownership
with communities being fully in power of the

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.329
future of what happens in their community
and I think that is something that everyone

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:37.420
in Canterbury will celebrate.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:43.010
The land divestment will see 70 hectares of
formerly red-zoned residential land in Kaiapoi

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:48.499
moved into the ownership of Council and 5
hectares in The Pines Beach and Kairaki transferred

00:00:48.499 --> 00:00:49.899
to the Trust.

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:54.480
This will allow the projects in the Waimakariri
Red Zone Recovery Plan to proceed and the

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.479
Minister noted the extensive community involvement
in the plan and praised the resilience of

00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:00.479
the local people.

00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:07.750
I want to acknowledge the people of Waimakariri,
who have shown over the last 8 years what

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.360
is possible as you have journeyed from recovery
to regeneration.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.140
Work has already begun in the regeneration
areas with the community establishment of

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:21.540
a Food Forest and a new roading link in the
east close to completion.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.890
With the recent approval of Regeneration funding
in the Council’s Long Term Plan, most recreational

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.100
projects are expected to be completed in the
next two to three years.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:37.000
We put aside $18 million over several years
for Regeneration areas in Kaiapoi and it’s

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.280
all going forward now, along with the work
we’re doing on the riverbank right this very minute.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:50.840
Other projects include a dog park, BMX track,
sports fields, mahinga kai and heritage areas,

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.280
and following today’s ceremony, the next
few years will see exciting progress

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.160
for the Waimakariri District.

